{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation complete (commit df34119e02e, pending Gerrit review).\n\nDiscipline: held-out TDD — 4 oracle tests written and proven RED first, fixer\nimplemented blind from the contract, oracle GREEN on first contact. Mutation\nchecks: allowlist key re-stripped, merge() list handling reverted, message\nrendering dropped — each went RED; restored fix GREEN.\n\nIndependent seam review (subagent, read-only) found one residual bug IN this\nfix: the message-rendering gate required all six format_repetition fields\nnon-None, but usage_log guarantees distinct_ratio_window is None below 24 tool\ncalls — so every short-run exhaustion (e.g. token exhaustion at 10 calls)\nrecreated the computed-then-discarded defect. Fixed RED-first: ratio dropped\nfrom the gate, None rendered as n/a(<window). Second review finding (recovery\nprelude show_ticket outside the diagnostic-capturing try, in merged fd84 code)\nfiled as 215f-92ab-9780-443d, discovered_from this ticket.\n\nLive Bedrock proof (exp_i_8b97_live.py): two GENUINE UsageLimitExceeded runs on\nhaiku-4-5 driven through the real interpret_failure -> CompletionAgentStep ->\nraise_completion_workflow_failure chain:\n- LONG (26 requests, 250 tool calls, ratio 0.375): repetition line rendered\n  with real values; sidecar carries aggregate_* keys; no tool arguments leak.\n- SHORT (2 requests, 6 tool calls, ratio None BY DESIGN): line still renders\n  with n/a(<window); no literal None anywhere.\nBoth regimes PASS all checks.\n\nGates: lint clean, mypy clean, targeted 37 passed; full marker suite matches\nthe pre-existing red baseline (verifying exact file list before push)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785974007115220001,"uuid":"d7b13d67-4295-4302-9e4e-22effa3dcc4e"}